KNOWNBUG
real_to_bool1.sv

^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p2\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p3\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p4\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p5\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p6\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p7\] .*: PROVED .*$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
All of these are REFUTED, including p0 and p1. verilog_lowering_cast
converts a real to bool like a real to an integer, giving
floatbv_typecast(floatbv_round_to_integral(3.0, ...), bool, ...)
(see --show-formula), which the solver does not evaluate as "nonzero".
With --smt2, the conversion fails an invariant.
